<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's net reserves rise to $2.11 bln in May.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's net reserves rise to $2.11 bln in May.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Tuesday its net international reserves grew 3.12 percent or $64 million to $2.11 billion in May.</p>
<p>In May 1996, international reserves stood at $1.54 billion.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of 1996, up $274 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
